The '''Popular Front''' ({{langx|bl|Frente Popular}}) was a pact formed in January 1920 by various [[W:Left-wing politics|left-wing political]] organizations during the [[Processo Revolucionario en Curso]], first to confront the growing [[Right-wing insurgency in Balisca|right-wing counterrevolution]] of the 1920s, and later as an [[W:Electoral alliance|electoral alliance]] during the [[W:Great Depression|Great Depression]] and subsequent [[Estau Nuevo|''Estau Nuevo'']] period. 

The [[1933 Confederal Convention]] determined that, in response to the growth of [[W:Fascism|fascism]] overseas, [[W:Popular front|popular fronts]] bringing together communists, anarchists and other leftists with other [[W:Anti-fascism|anti-fascists]] including Socialist and even [[W:Bourgeoisie|bourgeois]] were advisable. This led to a coalition between leftist republicans and workers' organizations to defend social reforms of the revolutionary government (PREC), and guide the confederal policy of rearmament in [[W:Causes of World War II|anticipation of war]].

